course: dictionary
lesson: 15437
title: Statute: a written law
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A statute is a law that has been written down. It is passed by a parliament or government, and then everyone must follow it. The word is formal, so you will mostly meet it in legal, civics or history texts. «The new statute made it compulsory to wear a seatbelt in the car.» The clue words written down and passed tell you what it means.
explain: Statute can also mean a written rule of an organisation, such as a university. «The university statute says students must hand in their work on time.» Here it is not a law from parliament. It is an official rule that the university has written down and expects everyone to keep.
explain: Look at the words around it. Written, passed, parliament, government and rule all point to an official meaning. If you swap in the word rule and the sentence still makes sense, you are on the right track. A statute is a special kind of rule, because it is written down and formally agreed.
fact: A statute is a law that has been written down and passed by a parliament or government.
fact: Statutes are different from old customs, which are ways of doing things that people have followed for a long time without writing them down.
fact: A statute can also be a written rule of an organisation, such as a university.
fact: «By statute» means according to a written law, and the «statute book» is where written laws are kept.
fact: The plural of statute is statutes.
exercise: «The new statute made it compulsory to wear a seatbelt.» What is a statute here? | A kind of pet | A story told by grandparents | A type of game | *A law that has been written down and passed
exercise: «The school statute says every pupil must wear a name badge.» What kind of statute is this? | A school holiday | *A written rule of an organisation | A nickname for the head teacher | A law passed by parliament
exercise: Which phrase means according to a written law? | *by statute | by mistake | by chance | by custom
test: «The new statute made it compulsory to wear a seatbelt.» Which statement is true? | *It is a written law that people must follow | It is a rule nobody has to keep | It is always a story told at bedtime | It is a type of bird
test: What is the plural of statute? | *statutes | statute's | statutus | statutee
exam: Which best describes a statute? | A rule that has never been written down | *A written rule or law that has been formally agreed | A famous painting in a museum | A spoken custom passed down by families
